Using data samples of 983.0~$m fb^{-1}$ and 427.9~$m fb^{-1}$ accumulated with the Belle and Belle~II detectors operating at the KEKB and SuperKEKB asymmetric-energy $e^+e^-$ colliders, singly Cabibbo-suppressed decays $Ξ_c^{+} 	o pK_{S}^{0}$, $Ξ_c^+ 	o Λπ^+$, and $Ξ_c^+ 	o Σ^{0} π^+$ are observed for the first time. The ratios of branching fractions of $Ξ_{c}^{+}	o p K_{S}^{0}$, $Ξ_{c}^{+}	o Λπ^{+}$, and $Ξ_{c}^{+}	o Σ^{0} π^{+}$ relative to that of $Ξ_c^+ 	o Ξ^- π^{+} π^{+}$ are measured to be  egin{equation}  rac{{\cal B}(Ξ_c^+ 	o pK_S^0)}{{\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Ξ^{-} π^+ π^+)} = (2.47 \pm 0.16 \pm 0.07)\% 
otag, \end{equation}  egin{equation}  rac{{\cal B}(Ξ_c^+ 	o Λπ^+)}{{\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Ξ^{-} π^+ π^+)} = (1.56 \pm 0.14 \pm 0.09)\% 
otag, \end{equation}  egin{equation}  rac{{\cal B}(Ξ_c^+ 	o Σ^0 π^+)}{{\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Ξ^{-} π^+ π^+)} = (4.13 \pm 0.26 \pm 0.22)\% 
otag. \end{equation} Multiplying these values by the branching fraction of the normalization channel, ${\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Ξ^{-} π^+π^+) = (2.9 \pm 1.3)\%$, the absolute branching fractions are determined to be  egin{equation} {\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o p K_{S}^{0}) = (7.16 \pm 0.46 \pm 0.20 \pm 3.21) 	imes 10^{-4} 
otag, \end{equation}  egin{equation} {\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Λπ^+) = (4.52 \pm 0.41 \pm 0.26 \pm 2.03) 	imes 10^{-4} 
otag, \end{equation}  egin{equation} {\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Σ^0 π^+) = (1.20 \pm 0.08 \pm 0.07 \pm 0.54) 	imes 10^{-3} 
otag. \end{equation} The first and second uncertainties above are statistical and systematic, respectively, while the third ones arise from the uncertainty in ${\cal B}(Ξ_c^{+} 	o Ξ^{-} π^{+} π^{+})$.
